Add visible build stamp + cache-busting PWA update (build 20261124-1100)

Why: the deploy-crash fix was verified in a clean browser but a browser
holding an old service worker keeps serving the old bundle, so it looks
like the update never landed. There was no way to tell which build was
actually running.

- vite: inject __BUILD_ID__ / __BUILD_DATE__ at build time, and derive the
  Workbox cacheId (`wrt-<buildid>`) + manifest name from it. Every deploy
  now gets a unique cache id, so Workbox installs a fresh cache and
  cleanupOutdatedCaches drops the old one.
- vite: skipWaiting + clientsClaim so a new SW takes control immediately
  instead of waiting for every tab to close.
- src/buildInfo.ts: BUILD_ID / BUILD_DATE / BUILD_LABEL helpers plus
  forceRefresh(), which unregisters all service workers, deletes every
  cache and hard-reloads.
- MainMenu footer: shows BUILD_LABEL + raw id (hover for the date).
- Settings: shows the build stamp and a "Force Refresh (clear cached
  build)" escape hatch for when a stale cache is stuck.
- Untrack nothing else; dist is still gitignored.

Build stamp for this build: BUILD 20261124-1100 (20261124110047).
If the menu footer does not show this string, the browser is running a
cached build — use Settings > Force Refresh.